+## 2026-08-22
+
+### 1853 — A pinned parent environment is what makes a captured env diff portable
+- DECISION: The launch-surface goldens (`pkg/agentic/parity/testdata/goldens/`) were captured by running the EXTRACTION SOURCE's own `TestCaptureLaunchSurface` under `env -i` with a synthetic parent environment, not under an ordinary shell. The source harness diffs the child env against `os.Environ()`; its own `parity-after.json` therefore carries `TASK_BOARD_BOARD_DIR=/Users/alexis/src/relux-works/skill-project-management/.task-board` and this session's run ids. `.scripts/capture-parity-goldens.sh`.
+- FINDING: The real defect an unpinned capture hides is not the leaked paths, it is the SILENCE. `env_removed` can only report a key the parent actually had. A plugin's strip of `CODEX_SESSION` or `TASK_BOARD_SESSION_ID` is provable only on a machine that happened to set it — everywhere else the golden records nothing and the port passes for want of evidence. The pinned set seeds exactly the keys `filterCodexRuntimeEnv`, `filterQwenRuntimeEnv` and `withSpawnEnv` act on, so each strip and each replacement is observable. `TASK_BOARD_DIR` is deliberately absent so the child's injection of it shows up as an addition.
+- DECISION: Each golden records its own `capture.parent_env`, and `ComparePlan` feeds THAT to the plan rather than letting the caller supply one. Env added/removed is a diff; a port supplying its own baseline compares a different measurement wearing the same schema. `TestAPlanBuiltWithoutTheGoldensParentEnvIsNotSilentlyAccepted`.
+- DECISION: PATH pinned to a stub-executable directory, so the dry-run cases resolve deterministically. Deviates from the source's artifact, which recorded its operator's installed codex and `executable file not found` for qwen/muse. An `error` fixture pins a refusal instead of the dry-run argv grammar — which is the thing the ports must reproduce — so the deviation buys the contract back. Written up in the fixtures README rather than left for a reader to hit.
+- FINDING: Masking must be ONE implementation used by both sides. Generation discovers the machine-local literals (`DiscoverSubstitutions`, regex over the capture layout) and then calls the SAME `Mask` the comparison calls. A regex masker at generation and a literal masker at comparison would agree until the day they did not, and the disagreement would read as a port bug.
+- NOTE: Three pins on masking, because masking is where a real difference goes invisible while the suite stays green: rule set frozen as a literal; the set of snapshot FIELDS masking may rewrite frozen and checked by planting a maskable literal in every field at once; each rule narrowed one at a time until a real golden stops matching. `pkg/agentic/parity/mask_test.go`.
+- SCOPE: `pkg/agentic/parity/` (new package, 14 goldens, 45 tests), `.scripts/capture-parity-goldens.sh`, `README.md`. Source checkout read-only throughout — one `go test`, clean before and after.
+- STATUS: TASK-260822-slgewd handed to review, uncommitted for the CR snapshot. Source commit pinned in every fixture: `ed4878123061b39fdae67160f6b5632117b48a2f`.
+
